{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113049","id":3036343645,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc60-u1d","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113049","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113049.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113049.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113049","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113049/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/113049/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113049/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b9c6c854445f9f899f1311348f386d5aebfc8efe","number":113049,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix `OS_LinuxBSD::get_video_adapter_driver_info()`: get IDs from currently selected graphics card","user":{"login":"MJacred","id":6639237,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzkyMzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6639237?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred","html_url":"https://github.com/MJacred","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MJacred/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"TODOs\r\n* [x] get driver name\r\n* [x] implement for compatibility mode\r\n  * [x] stop crashing when calling this func\r\n  * see `godot/drivers/gles3/storage/utilities.cpp`, change implementation to be analogous to `get_maximum_viewport_size` to avoid crash\r\n  * update: calling `clGetDeviceInfo` with `CL_DEVICE_VENDOR_ID` as info should return the vendor id, and the device id is in `basisu::ocl::get_device_id()` in file `encoder/basisu_opencl.cpp`, but it's not accessible. re-doing the steps (see ´clGetDeviceIDs`) should provide the device ID\r\n    * ~~for now, I'll bring back and improve the previous logic for gles3 as a fallback~~\r\n    * getting driver name: improve guesswork in case of multiple cards\r\n      * _or_ use `glxinfo -B` and read the lines  `Vendor:` and `Device:`, they contain the device IDs (dunno what `glxinfo` spits out when there are multiple cards\r\n    * getting the version: `uname -r` (**6.14.0-35-generic**) + the result of using `glxinfo` (**Mesa 25.0.7**): `6.14.0-35-generic | Mesa 25.0.7`\r\n      * steps: `glxinfo -B | grep \"OpenGL renderer string\"` returns `Mesa Intel(R) Arc(tm) Graphics (MTL)`. String splitting based on vendor name is too risky (because they are never consistent), so we take our chances and split on the first space. And by using `$ glxinfo -B | grep \"Version\"` we get the rest: `25.0.7`\r\n\r\n* `modinfo` does not provide driver version\r\n  * not sure if fixable. might be a limitation on some GPUs/drivers\r\n    * known affected systems\r\n      *  `Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS 24.04 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated Intel(R) Arc(tm) Graphics (MTL) (i915)`\r\n  * proposal: use `glxinfo` as seen above\r\n\r\nfixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112788","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_